  "Description": "The Visual Salience Mapping (PGM-VSM) AIM is a Sub-AIM of Visual Scene Enhancement (PGM-VSE). It determines the relative perceptual importance of Visual Objects with respect to user interaction and context, and produces the Salient Object Matrix. Each Sub-AIM of Visual Scene Enhancement independently generates a Visual CXT Response, a Visual Domain Request and a Visual Interaction History Request. Visual Enhancement Multiplexing multiplexes them into the corresponding external output signals of Visual Scene Enhancement. [High-level specification derived from the Visual Scene Enhancement page. ",
